============================================================================
WHAT THAT DOES TO THE PREVIOUS PASS
============================================================================
  The 1.81% shift the earlier pass borrowed from the fit is real ONLY if the winding
  is short enough for a partial turn to matter. The envelope above puts that at
  roughly N < 20 turns; past a few tens of turns f_bar is pinned to 2/pi far tighter
  than the 2.08% conflict, and the escape closes.

  So branch (a) does not rest on 'the fit disagrees with 2/pi' -- that is noise around
  a theorem. It rests on whether the winding completes enough turns, which is a
  physical question with a recorded answer elsewhere in the corpus, and a different
  question from the one the fit's scatter answers.

  Stated as a requirement: closing the alpha_c conflict through f_bar needs the
  winding to be short. Solving the envelope for a 2.08% worst case gives
  N = 4.8 turns -- and note the 1/(pi N) proxy would have said 15, overstating
  the allowance by a factor of three. Anything longer than a handful of turns
  leaves the conflict standing at close to its full 2.08%.
